# Applies to docker/backend/Dockerfile and docker/worker/Dockerfile, whose
# build context is the repo root (see docker-compose.yml). Keeps the context
# sent to the Docker daemon limited to what those images actually need
# (backend/, ai/) — everything below is either irrelevant to those images or
# already excluded by their own COPY lines, so shipping it as build context
# would only slow builds down.

.git/
.github/

frontend/
docker/

docs/
database/
*.md
# backend/pyproject.toml's `readme = "../README.md"` is read by hatchling's
# build backend even for an editable install (see docker/backend/Dockerfile's
# `COPY README.md /srv/README.md` comment) — excluding it here would make
# that explicit COPY fail with a build-context "file not found".
!README.md

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
backend/.venv/
backend/.coverage

# Env/secrets — never send real .env files into a build context
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
